---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CardDemo from '../components/CardDemo.astro';
import { brand, link } from '../config';
---
<Base>
  <main id="content">
    <section class="opening"><div class="opening-margin"><span>01 / A daily practice</span><span>Personal, by design</span></div><div class="opening-title"><h1>Make room<br/>for <em>what stays.</em></h1><div class="opening-bottom"><p>Your Anki decks, a quieter place to study.<br/>Return to what you’re learning, wherever<br class="desktop-break"/> the day takes you.</p><a class="button primary" href={link('docs/self-host/')}>Build your study space <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div><div class="opening-note"><span>Bring your decks.<br/>Keep your rhythm.</span><span>↓ A little further</span></div></section>
    <div class="practice-section" data-reveal><div class="practice-intro"><p class="index-label">02 / The art of returning</p><h2>Not everything<br/>needs <em>more.</em><br/>Some things<br/>need <em>again.</em></h2><p>A question. A moment to remember. An answer. Rate your recall, and FSRS schedules the next review.</p><p>Languages, science, history, the things you want to keep. There’s room for all of them.</p></div><CardDemo/></div>
    <section class="ownership-section" data-reveal><div><p class="index-label">03 / Yours to keep</p><h2>A personal library.<br/><em>With your name on it.</em></h2></div><div class="ownership-copy"><p class="large-copy">Your own installation. Your own collection. One shared learning history across the devices you connect.</p><p>{brand} is software you run for yourself. Clone the source, choose a local server or Cloudflare Pages with Supabase, then import the decks you already have.</p><a class="text-link" href={link('docs/architecture/')}>See how it fits together <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="ownership-ledger"><div><span>Bring along</span><strong>Anki .apkg</strong><p>Basic cards, simple cloze, images, audio, and nested decks.</p></div><div><span>Keep in reach</span><strong>Phone & computer</strong><p>A browser is all you need. Cloud study requires a connection.</p></div><div><span>Take with you</span><strong>Decks & progress</strong><p>Download a cloud backup with your collection and media.</p></div></div></section>
    <section class="handbook-section" data-reveal><div><p class="index-label">04 / Leave the door open</p><h2>Start small.<br/><em>Make it yours.</em></h2><p>Run it locally first, or give it a home online.<br/>The handbook walks through both.</p><a class="button primary" href={link('docs/')}>Open the handbook <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="chapter-list"><a href={link('docs/self-host/')}><span>01</span><div><h3>Host your own</h3><p>Set up your installation, step by step.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href={link('docs/compatibility/')}><span>02</span><div><h3>Bring the right decks</h3><p>Check compatibility before you import.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href={link('docs/devices-backups/')}><span>03</span><div><h3>Connect & keep a copy</h3><p>Pair devices and back up your collection.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="honest-note"><span>One thing to know</span><p>This is an independent study app. It imports supported Anki decks, but does not sync with AnkiWeb or reproduce every Anki feature. <a href={link('docs/compatibility/')}>Read the current limits.</a></p></section>
  </main>
</Base>
